xnu 0358: name the check that marks the volume, and the blocks a failed free claims

`hfs_mark_inconsistent()` prints one generic line and sets the inconsistent bit,
so every call dirties the volume header and forces fsck. A boot on the repaired
root produced 370 of those lines with only two failed frees, and most call sites
print nothing of their own: the ring says the volume went inconsistent without
saying which check found what.

Three additions, all silent unless something is already wrong:

- every call carries its function and line (a macro in hfs.h, the function
  itself in hfs_vfsops.c), printing the first occurrence of each site and then
  every hundredth, so one boot lists the live sites instead of flooding;
- the budget check in hfs_catalog.c prints the cnid, the name and both block
  counts of the file whose catalog record claims more than its extents hold:
  that is the one mark that fires on ordinary lookups and it says nothing today;
- a failed free lists the allocations of this boot that overlap the range, so
  "free unallocated blocks" reads either as a double allocation or as a mark
  that never reached the bitmap.

